==Overview==
<tabber>
Pros=
{{Overview|Pros
|'''General'''
* Extremely high damage.
* Good combo potential.
* Good knockback, which is useful in PvP.
* Both moves [[break Instinct]].
* Insane damage in short duration, making [[Shark]] and [[Cyborg (race)|Cyborg]] users take a lot of damage before they can turn on their Race ability.

|'''[Z] Demon Slayer'''
* Dash is very fast.
* Almost no end lag.
* Can target multiple players.
* Damage is still dealt as long as the target has been caught in the dash (Unless "[[Instinct]]-Tricked").
* Deals damage over time.
* Good range.
* Can stun [[Blade]] users along with [[Saishi]].

|'''[X] Burning Slash'''
* The flames [[break Instinct]].
* [[Breaks Instinct]] on direct contact.
* Decent [[AoE]] when held.
* No end-lag.
}}

|-|Cons=
{{Overview|Cons
|'''General'''
* Cannot damage [[Blade]] users.
* Low drop chance for the [[Hidden Key]].
* Bad for in-water combat.
* Difficult to grind due to dashing from the fourth slash.
* High mastery requirements.

|'''[Z] Demon Slayer'''
* Single target. (Though the flames can damage nearby enemies if they are close)

|'''[X] Burning Slash'''
* The flame trail can be dodged easily if not stunned.
* This move, along with its two variations, does not have any [[AoE]] burn when used aerially, making it significantly harder to hit (the tap variation works similarly and has a similar hitbox to awakened [[Dark]]'s {{Ability|Dark|Z|1}}, the held variation works the same, just vertically).
}}
</tabber>

==Trivia==
* Rengoku is an [[Easter Eggs|easter egg]] that the devs added at [[Updates/13|Update 13]].
* Before the rework in [[Updates/20|Update 20]], {{Ability|Z}} did not do burn damage. 
* Rengoku's moveset post-rework is similar to the [[Pipe]].
* Rengoku is the only katana to be out of its hilt in its icon. 
* {{Ability|Z}} can sometimes glitch the player out of the map if the flooring is thin like in [[Kingdom of Rose]].
